  "lineage": "Late-1960s-and-1970s rock subgenre integrating extended psychedelic instrumental passages with science-fiction-cosmic thematic content. Hawkwind (UK 1969-onward) inaugurated the canonical style with Space Ritual (1973); Pink Floyd's pre-Dark-Side material, Gong's Radio Gnome Invisible trilogy, and (in the 1980s revival) Spacemen 3 and Loop continued the lineage. Distinguished from broader progressive rock by space rock's specific psychedelic-cosmic thematic focus and extended-instrumental-passage emphasis.",
